--------------------------------------------------------------------
Introduction
--------------------------------------------------------------------

This is an intermediate release, initially shipped as a binary
distribution for Windows 95 and NT.  A source release will be made
available before the end of this month.

The PIL handbook is available via http://www.pythonware.com
(currently as HTML only).

News highlights in 0.3b1 (as compared to 0.2b4):

+ Uses memory mapping to read some uncompressed formats
  (currently on Win32 only).

+ The "save" method now automatically converts images on the fly
  in some cases.  This includes converting "1" to "L" (JPEG) and
  "RGBA" to "RGB" (JPEG, PPM, BMP).

+ Support 32-bit integer and floating point images.

+ The Tk interface now supports transparent images.
  *** NOTE: the Tk interface has been changed; you need to update
  *** your Tkinter build to properly handle the new interface.

+ Added read support for McIdas, Pixar Raster, FlashPix (FPX),
  IPTC/NAA and Microsoft Image Composer (MIC).

+ Fixed the FLI/FLC reader to properly read FLC files.

+ Fixed the PDF writer.  It now properly writes "L" and "RGB"
  images.

+ Lots of bug fixes.

For more information on these and other changes, see the CHANGES
document.

For installation and licensing details, see below.

For questions, comments and bug reports, send mail to
'image-sig@python.org'.


